From 512f93867f7bfb45cb7ab0990265040eb7ed0675 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:34:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): reuse the replica read while hub.db task rows
 are unchanged [daveey]

The sidebar's remote-links projection rebuilds on every local board write, and each rebuild re-read all ~6k
replica task rows (~23 MB) from hub.db even though they change only when a hub pull lands (hub.db's WAL itself
moves ~45x/min from outbox/cursor writes, so a file-stat key would not help).

_read_remote_links now keys a memo on an index-only probe of the task rows (count, max/total seq, total version,
total octet_length) plus identity, heartbeat and meta rows, read in the same transaction as the rows; hermes-hub
stamps every replica write with a new feed seq. Reuse also ends at the next stale/heartbeat cut-off. Explicit
`now`, seq-less replicas and NULL seqs always read. _project_remote_links indexes receipt rows for `superseded`
instead of scanning all of them per legacy card.

Live replay, 30 polls: remote projection 49 -> 25 ms/poll, replica read 34 -> 13 ms/poll; 79/79 memoized reads
identical to explicit-now reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
